<!--
  RUT_Fuzz.xml                         COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 (partial pass,
                                        arid_shrubland sheet)

  The arid shrubland's dominant flora. FROZEN sheet:
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/arid_shrubland.md §4 "The giants":

    "The fuzz is graze-adapted: growth crown buried below the soil line, leaves
    expendable. The lawn and the mowers are one equilibrium - the giants
    maintain the very openness that makes them safe." Also §1/description:
    "Knee-high silver-green fuzz at eerily even spacing, running unbroken to
    every horizon, all of it leaning the same way, all of it moving - because
    the wind never stops."

  Slug (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, arid_shrubland sheet):
  `the-fuzz-knee-high-silver-green-canopy-plant`. Re-verified currency
  2026-09-21 against infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} and
  src/ before authoring - nothing existing matched "fuzz"/"silver-green"/
  "canopy". rosters/arid_shrubland.json's own "new_defs" entry flags this
  slug's mechanic_load as "none blocking" (a pure flora commission, not a
  mechanics ask) and its own "flora" list already documents
  `Plant_ShrubLow` (vanilla low shrubs) as "the knee-high fuzz stand-in
  UNTIL THE FUZZ DEF LANDS" at 0.9 commonality in RUT_AridShrubland.xml -
  this def is that landing, and RUT_AridShrubland.xml's wildPlants entry is
  swapped from Plant_ShrubLow to this def at the same 0.9 weight.

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED. arid_shrubland.md's own "Owed" section lists
  "the fuzz itself" among the names still the owner's pick (alongside the
  giants, the snake-analogs, the bird-analogs, venomvine, and the Stall/Gale
  weather names). `RUT_Fuzz` is the INTERNAL working defName and every label
  below is provisional, same pattern as RUT_Staggerseed
  (STAGGERSEED_SHIPPING_NAME_1) - renaming later is one def plus one
  wildPlants line. No separate owner card filed for this one name alone;
  folded into the arid_shrubland naming sweep this pass also opened,
  `ARIDSHRUBLAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1` (covers the fuzz, tunnel-snake and the
  huge grazer flagship built this same pass).

  ART: one job filed this pass, `rutfuzz_v1`
  (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/rutfuzz_v1.json) - silver-green, wind-combed,
  matted low fronds per arid_shrubland.md §9's palette. Art is name-free (same
  reasoning as RUT_Staggerseed's own comment): nothing about the render
  depends on which name the owner eventually picks.

  Ban check against arid_shrubland.md §6: ban 9 ("no flammable living flora")
  - Flammability 0 on this def directly, no reliance on
  BiomeFloraStatAdjustments_Generated.xml since this is our own def, not a
  donor mod's. No other ban in §6 touches a low groundcover plant.

  MECHANIC: "graze-adapted crown-below-soil" is flavour text on this pass -
  mechanic_load reads "none blocking" and nothing in the biome doc's own
  "engine feasibility pass owed" list names this plant, unlike the giants'
  life-stage/enrage or venomvine's passability. Represented here only as a
  fast regrowDays and a low harvestWork (the crown surviving underneath is
  why it comes back quickly), not as new C#.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RUT_Fuzz</defName>
    <label>the fuzz</label>
    <description>A dense mat of fine silver-green fronds, never taller than the knee, combed permanently in one direction by a wind that never stops. Its growth crown sits below the soil line, so grazing and cutting alike only ever take the expendable leaves above - the fuzz and the giants that mow it are one equilibrium, and it is back within days.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>0.15</Nutrition>
      <Beauty>0</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- Job rutfuzz_v1, filed this pass. Pending until the daemon lands it. -->
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RUT_Fuzz</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.35, 0.15, 0.15)</volume>
        <offset>(0,0,-0.2)</offset>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <neverMultiSelect>false</neverMultiSelect>
    <fillPercent>0.15</fillPercent>
    <pathCost>8</pathCost>
    <ingestible>
      <foodType>VegetableOrFruit</foodType>
      <preferability>RawBad</preferability>
    </ingestible>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.25</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.4</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>6</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <maxMeshCount>4</maxMeshCount>
      <visualSizeRange>0.55~0.85</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>1.0</topWindExposure>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <harvestYield>2</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>40</harvestWork>
      <harvestAfterGrowth>0.3</harvestAfterGrowth>
      <wildClusterRadius>6</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>60</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildEqualLocalDistribution>true</wildEqualLocalDistribution>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <purpose>Misc</purpose>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
